# Admin Credentials Template

## Default Admin Account

**Username:** `admin`  
**Password:** See `docker-compose.yml` environment or your deployment secrets  
**Email:** `admin@indiestack.local`

---

## Security Note

**NEVER commit actual credentials to git!**

1. Copy this file to create your local credentials doc (not tracked by git):
   ```bash
   cp ADMIN_CREDENTIALS.md.example ADMIN_CREDENTIALS.md.local
   ```

2. Add `ADMIN_CREDENTIALS.md.local` to your `.gitignore`

3. For production, use environment variables or a secrets manager (Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, etc.)

---

## Default Test Credentials (Development Only)

After running seed data:

| Username | Email | Password | Role |
|----------|-------|----------|------|
| admin | admin@indiestack.local | (set via ADMIN_PASSWORD env var) | Admin |
| alice | alice@example.com | (use registration) | Writer |
| bob | bob@example.com | (use registration) | Creator |

---

## Register a New User

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/v1/auth/register \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "email": "test@example.com",
    "username": "testuser",
    "password": "password123",
    "display_name": "Test User"
  }'
```

---

*This file is an example template. Do not add real credentials here.*
